(e) Parking lot: Space to park at least 10 passenger cars;
(f) Other amenities: A lounge and toilets available to applicants. Separate toilets shall be provided for men and women.

Note: If rights to use equipment and facilities are secured through a lease agreement or similar arrangement and this is proved by documents, the relevant equipment and facilities shall be deemed provided for the term of that agreement.

■ Enforcement Decree of the Water Leisure Safety Act [Annex 10]
Detailed Standards for Revocation of Designation and Suspension of Services of Examination Agencies (Related to Article 18 (1))

1. General standards
(a) If there are two or more violations and their respective disposition standards differ, the heavier disposition standard shall apply. If two or more disposition standards all require suspension of services, the heavier disposition standard shall be increased by up to one-half, without exceeding the sum of the periods under the respective disposition standards.
(b) Standards for administrative dispositions based on the number of violations shall apply where an administrative disposition (including a disposition imposing a penalty surcharge; hereinafter the same shall apply in this Annex) has been received for the same violation within the most recent 1 year. The period shall be calculated by reference to the date the administrative disposition was received for the violation and the date on which the same violation committed again after that disposition was detected.
(c) When imposing an aggravated administrative disposition under item (b), the applicable violation level shall be the level immediately following that of the disposition preceding the violation concerned (the highest level if two or more administrative dispositions were imposed within the period under item (b)).
(d) The authority imposing the disposition may reduce the suspension period under the individual standards in paragraph 2 by up to one-half in any of the following cases:
1) Where the violation is recognized as resulting from minor negligence or error;
2) Where the violator immediately corrects or remedies the violation and thereby ends the state of noncompliance with the Act;
3) Where a reduction of the suspension period is otherwise considered necessary in view of the nature, severity, motive, consequences, or other circumstances of the violation.
(e) The authority imposing the disposition may increase the suspension period under the individual standards in paragraph 2 by up to one-half in any of the following cases. Even when increased, the suspension period shall not exceed 6 months:
1) Where the nature and severity of the violation are serious and the harm to users or others is recognized as substantial;
2) Where the state of noncompliance with the Act has lasted at least 6 months;
3) Where an increase in the suspension period is otherwise considered necessary in view of the severity, motive, consequences, or other circumstances of the violation.

