■ Enforcement Decree of the Water Leisure Safety Act [Annex 14] <Amended on June 2, 2025>
Standards for Imposing Administrative Fines (Related to Article 39)

1. General standards
(a) Aggravated standards for imposing administrative fines based on the number of violations shall apply where a disposition imposing an administrative fine has been received for the same violation within the most recent 1 year. The period shall be calculated by reference to the date the disposition imposing an administrative fine was received for the violation and the date on which the same violation committed again after that disposition was detected.
(b) When imposing an aggravated fine under item (a), the applicable violation level shall be the level immediately following that of the disposition preceding the violation concerned (the highest level if two or more dispositions imposing administrative fines were imposed within the period under item (a)).
(c) The imposing authority may reduce the administrative fine under the individual standards in paragraph 2 by up to one-half in any of the following cases. This shall not apply to a violator in arrears with administrative fines:
1) Where the violation is recognized as resulting from minor negligence or error;
2) Where the violator is recognized as having made efforts to correct or end the state of noncompliance with the Act;
3) Where a reduction in the administrative fine is otherwise considered necessary in view of the severity, motive, consequences, or other circumstances of the violation.
(d) The imposing authority may increase the administrative fine under the individual standards in paragraph 2 by up to one-half in any of the following cases. Even when increased, the fine shall not exceed the maximum administrative fine under Article 64 (1) and (2) of the Act:
1) Where the nature and severity of the violation are serious and the harm to users or others is recognized as substantial;
2) Where the state of noncompliance with the Act has lasted at least 6 months;
3) Where an increase in the administrative fine is otherwise considered necessary in view of the severity, motive, consequences, or other circumstances of the violation.

